WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:03.429
- [Announcer] Please
welcome Drew Barrymore.

00:00:03.429 --> 00:00:05.459
(inspiring music)

00:00:05.459 --> 00:00:06.876
- Ahh! This is...

00:00:08.059 --> 00:00:08.892
Hi!

00:00:10.339 --> 00:00:12.211
Oh my God, Ahh!

00:00:12.211 --> 00:00:13.629
It's happening, it's real.

00:00:13.629 --> 00:00:16.629
Welcome to the Drew Barrymore Show.

00:00:16.629 --> 00:00:20.630
It's Monday, my favorite day

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:22.730
'cause we're here to rebrand Mondays.

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:25.260
Boy did they get the
short end of the deal.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:26.590
We love Mondays around here

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:28.610
because after obsessing over the weekend

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:30.810
about all the things you need to do,

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:34.950
I say, Monday's is the day to get her done

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:37.340
and look ahead to all the great things

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:39.223
that you can do this week.

00:00:40.252 --> 00:00:41.750
(audience cheering)
(big sigh)

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:42.700
My heart's beating.

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:48.760
Okay, now, allow me to reintroduce myself.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:52.573
You may think you know me and you do.

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:57.040
I am who you think I am,

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:00.450
but I'm also someone who
is learning all the time.

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:02.700
And I'm so excited to figure out

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:05.990
this thing called life with you.

00:01:05.990 --> 00:01:08.230
I believe in the collective experience,

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:09.770
and for my entire life,

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:12.400
I've been interacting with people,

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:16.310
and that's exactly what I
want to do on this show.

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:21.310
This is all for you.
(audience cheering)

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:25.050
It's true, as it says in
the opening of our show,

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:29.560
we're gonna learn, laugh,
cry, cook, heal, all of it.

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:33.650
And I'm committed to
putting all aspects of life

00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:36.230
into this show every day.

00:01:36.230 --> 00:01:40.739
Now, here we are in this studio,
we have our fantastic crew.

00:01:40.739 --> 00:01:42.408
I love you guys so much.

00:01:42.408 --> 00:01:44.650
(audience cheering)

00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:48.320
And look, in some ways
you're the physical audience

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:50.960
and you'll be hearing
them throughout our show

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:52.650
and hearing their wonderful cacophony,

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:55.627
bringing the life and energy to this room.

00:01:55.627 --> 00:01:56.770
(audience cheering)

00:01:56.770 --> 00:01:58.190
No pressure.

00:01:58.190 --> 00:02:01.468
And we also have our virtual friends.

00:02:01.468 --> 00:02:03.490
Hello!
(audience clapping)

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:07.250
Look at these humans in
this brand new technology,

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:08.750
but technology aside,

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:11.260
we found a new way to have
that collective experience

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:14.470
from people with all over
it, for all over the country.

00:02:14.470 --> 00:02:15.570
See it's live, whoops.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:19.523
So we'll see you guys throughout the show.

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:23.963
And to everyone else in my personal life,

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:28.400
thank you for watching today, I love you.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:31.133
And to my two daughters,
Olive and Frankie,

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:36.113
everything, all of it,
is always just for you.

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:39.010
So, let's get started everyone,

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:40.710
and the way we're going to start each show

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:43.752
is a segment called Drew's News.

00:02:43.752 --> 00:02:44.981
(audience cheering)

00:02:44.981 --> 00:02:47.470
(van crashing)
(cat squealing)

00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:51.537
(dramatic music)
Excuse me, sir, ma'am, guys!

00:02:53.092 --> 00:02:54.675
Tell me your story!

00:02:56.527 --> 00:03:00.180
Ma'am, I asked you a question.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:01.180
This is Drew's News!

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:05.503
This is Drew's News.

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:08.103
It's Drew's News.

00:03:09.821 --> 00:03:11.401
(audience cheering)

00:03:11.401 --> 00:03:12.234
At this desk, we're
going to curate all kinds

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:16.070
of stories for you.

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:20.350
I am a news and pop culture junkie.

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:22.290
I love good news.

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:26.750
I also like odd or unique
happenings that make me laugh.

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:30.220
I love hearing about
trends and hot topics.

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:31.850
I like to seek out the stories

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:33.440
that may be a little harder to find,

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:38.150
but are totally life affirming
and necessary to hear

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:41.010
because we all need to
know it's going to be okay.

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:44.940
So consider me your human
scrapbook full of stories,

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:48.063
both big, small, and
everything in between.

00:03:48.930 --> 00:03:52.000
Oh right. Our first
story is personal to us.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:54.288
Tonight, the Empire State
Building is lighting up

00:03:54.288 --> 00:03:58.546
in our signature yellow in
honor of our big premier.

00:03:58.546 --> 00:04:00.670
(audience cheering)
Ahh!

00:04:00.670 --> 00:04:02.670
And even though I'm a Cali girl at heart,

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:05.000
and I'm thinking of all
of you West coasters

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:09.030
during these fires, New
York is now my adopted home,

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:11.440
and this honor means so much to us.

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:13.150
Thank you, New York.

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:15.673
Now, let's see what made the papers.

00:04:15.673 --> 00:04:16.830
(audience clapping)

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:18.560
Okay. Oh, I love this story

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:22.600
because it made her-story.

00:04:22.600 --> 00:04:25.180
This year for the first
time three moms made it

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:26.950
to the quarterfinals,

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:30.493
Serena Williams, Tsvetana Pironkova,

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:33.583
and Victoria Azarenka.

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:36.620
I might've messed that up, and if so,

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:38.010
I am so sorry.

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:40.940
The winner was actually Naomi Osaka,

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:43.140
and I really just wanted to give it up

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:44.980
to all these incredible women.

00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:47.230
Shine a light on you,
as everyone is doing,

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:49.890
and celebrate you right
along everybody else.

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:51.840
Thank you for all that you're doing

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:53.893
and inspiring all of us moms.

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:57.960
Our third story, CNN reports

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:02.960
that a 62 year old ball
Python has laid seven eggs.

00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:06.510
Even though she hasn't
been near a male snake

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:08.930
in over two decades.

00:05:08.930 --> 00:05:11.950
Is she 62 are 16?

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:15.920
Sneaking out for a little fun, uh huh.

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:17.654
This story resonates with
me because I haven't been

00:05:17.654 --> 00:05:21.745
in captivity with a male
for quite some time either.

00:05:21.745 --> 00:05:24.410
Uhn uh, I have my two daughters
and my cup runneth over,

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:26.000
if you know what I mean, I'm good.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:29.760
However, when I usually fill
out medical forms and they ask,

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:31.796
is there a possibility you're pregnant?

00:05:31.796 --> 00:05:35.090
I'm usually like, not a chance,

00:05:35.090 --> 00:05:38.100
but now she's making me
rethink, and get scared,

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:40.060
and curious, and wonder.

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:43.770
Listen, this mama Python, she got it done.

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:46.650
And although it is
certainly suspicious how,

00:05:46.650 --> 00:05:50.222
I say, live your bliss.

00:05:50.222 --> 00:05:52.030
(audience clapping)

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:54.550
And finally, this one got me so excited

00:05:54.550 --> 00:05:55.830
because I love board games.

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:58.270
I mean, literally this is my game closet.

00:05:58.270 --> 00:06:00.250
There's no joke there.

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:03.850
And Toy Book magazine reports that Hasbro

00:06:03.850 --> 00:06:08.480
is making a Guess Who
Hometown Helpers edition.

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:12.660
A version of the game with
characters like firefighter,

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:15.443
and teacher, mail carrier, and more.

00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:21.750
Hasbro's also donating $10 per game sold

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:23.800
to community charities.

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:26.550
Does your person have
glasses and save lives?

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:28.853
Tk, tk, tk, tk, tk, yes.

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:32.540
One more story that I don't want to miss.

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:34.540
Actually, we've got two minutes to crush.

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:36.790
Oh my gosh, how did this happen?

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:39.080
Okay, so here we are.

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:43.070
It's our very first
show, and I am nervous,

00:06:43.070 --> 00:06:44.184
I'm excited.

00:06:44.184 --> 00:06:48.580
We're live in certain
places, so if I mess up,

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:49.780
well, you know what?

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:50.980
That's just going to happen.

00:06:50.980 --> 00:06:54.230
And all I can say is, I am so excited

00:06:54.230 --> 00:06:56.090
that we are here for day one,

00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:58.769
and we'll be right back with more.

00:06:58.769 --> 00:07:01.602
(inspiring music)

